## Overview

A challenging T4 hike with a consistently steep ascent. The final climb is very exposed, requires the use of hands and carries the risk of a fall of over 100 m. Not suitable for novice mountaineers.
It is advisable to check the weather forecast specifically for Monte Generosa.
We were caught in the rain during the most difficult section, which probably made it the most nerve-wracking hike of my life.

## How to get there

Travel by bus (line 541) to Rovio, Paese.
<JourneyPlanner from="<current location>" to="Rovio, Paese" toFixed target="arrival" time="09:00" />

## Start

You start in Rovio and take a moment to enjoy the village’s narrow lanes.
<HikeImage idx={0} />
<HikeImage idx={1} />

Then the first section through the forest begins. Initially, the route follows a fairly good forest track. Later, it transitions to a path with a much steeper ascent. The path is very well marked.
